Nice. I think in both my and Vince's answers, the key is using vectorized operations to get to simplify your life, i.e. either:

>z <100
and look for runs of 4 TRUES

OR,

>which(z < 100)
and look for runs of 4 consecutive numbers.

Given `rle` is in base, there's a good chance it's the faster route.

