6 is the FIRST value in the relevant run of four consecutive values < 100, 9 is the FOURTH value. Here's my attempt:
run_length <- 4
value_under <- 100
z <- c(150, 150, 99, 99, 150, 99, 99, 99, 99, 150, 150, 99, 99, 99, 99, 100)
rl <- rle(z)
run <- which(rl$values < value_under & rl$lengths >= run_length)[1]
OUT <- sum(rl$lengths[1:run])

